1
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kick a pebble and my shoes fly off too.

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,920
Onto the head of the
carpenter I was choking,

4
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:39,120
they laughed that I was still just a brat.

5
00:00:39,870 --> 00:00:44,200
Even if I somehow stir up some energy,

6
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:49,280
in Katsushika,
with one more yawn, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,180
The streets feel strangely kind.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,140
From the pointed hat and the ablution jug,

9
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:07,440
the setting sun sinks toward the horizon.

10
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow, it all ends like this, doesn't it.

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,120
In Katsushika and Shibamata,
I lose happiness again.

12
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:24,520
Because I'm a fool who finally realized it.

13
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:31,720
Mass-produced dolls, now on sale!

14
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:58,320
Ah ah ah

15
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:18,360
Ryo-san finally got his
first meal in three days.

16
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:55,080
Wait a moment, please.

17
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:57,140
H-hey, what's this?

18
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:59,100
I knew it.

19
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:02,540
What do you think you're doing?

20
00:03:02,540 --> 00:03:04,760
Cut it out, you creep!

21
00:03:05,780 --> 00:03:07,460
It's a doll, a doll!

22
00:03:07,940 --> 00:03:09,840
I want that doll.

23
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:10,960
A doll?

24
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:12,900
You mean this one?

25
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:14,320
Exactly.

26
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:16,580
This is an early-model Bardy,
a real treasure.

27
00:03:17,380 --> 00:03:17,820
Please.

28
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:19,960
Please sell this to me.

29
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:22,500
This crummy old doll?

30
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:23,940
I'll buy it at whatever price you name.

31
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:26,060
Name any price you like.

32
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:27,540
Deal, right?

33
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:34,720
For 500 yen,
you could buy a makunouchi bento!

34
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:36,720
So, five...

35
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:37,880
Fifty thousand yen?

36
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:40,940
If it's fifty thousand yen,
I'll pay in cash right away.

37
00:03:40,940 --> 00:03:43,160
Fifty thousand yen.

38
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:46,280
I had no idea that doll was so valuable.

39
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:51,500
Even Jiai-jō and I, a collector
of men's dolls, didn't know that.

40
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:52,840
Thank goodness.

41
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:57,480
I've got the complete set of
the new Birdie ponytail types!

42
00:03:57,900 --> 00:03:59,240
Man-chan is so happy.

43
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:02,360
You're a creepy one, aren't you.

44
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:03,980
Who exactly are you?

45
00:04:05,180 --> 00:04:05,900
Me?

46
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:08,060
I'm someone like this.

47
00:04:08,060 --> 00:04:09,580
A doll critic.

48
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:11,780
Since when is that a real job?

49
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:15,880
If you ever have a rare doll,
I'll take it off your hands anytime.

50
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:17,040
Please come visit me.

51
00:04:17,980 --> 00:04:20,860
Now hurry home,
and I'll clean you up nicely.

52
00:04:21,840 --> 00:04:24,760
I had no idea dolls
could make this much money.

53
00:04:27,580 --> 00:04:28,620
Still just food for now.

54
00:04:29,740 --> 00:04:32,280
Ryo-san got his hands on 50,000 yen.

55
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:46,020
Even though you're hungry,
how can you eat that much?

56
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:49,940
Even a gorilla couldn't eat this much.

57
00:04:50,860 --> 00:04:55,560
Get lost! You heartless jerk, you wouldn't
lend us a single yen when we were in trouble!

58
00:04:56,700 --> 00:04:57,168
Well, that's because...

59
00:04:57,218 --> 00:05:00,720
the Chief ordered us not to lend
Ryo-san so much as a single cent.

60
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:04,240
Do you two do anything
the Chief tells you to?!

61
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:10,960
Honestly, it's your fault, Ryo-chan, for
spending your paycheck the moment you get it!

62
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:12,480
What's all this fuss about?

63
00:05:13,060 --> 00:05:15,280
Chief, good morning.

64
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:18,120
Good morning, good morning.

65
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:22,560
Ryotsu!

66
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:25,600
What kind of person are you!

67
00:05:25,780 --> 00:05:29,280
You were supposed to be fasting for three days,
so what's this lavish meal?!

68
00:05:30,020 --> 00:05:32,140
Did you rob someone? Or shake someone down?!

69
00:05:32,260 --> 00:05:32,980
What?!

70
00:05:33,660 --> 00:05:35,720
W-wait, it's not what it looks like!
Please calm down!

71
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:38,600
Ryo-chan, tea, tea!

72
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:42,800
Whoa, I thought I was going to die!

73
00:05:44,700 --> 00:05:48,160
Hahaha pardon me, pardon me.

74
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:50,720
Me, a virtuous police officer,

75
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:54,020
would never steal or skim, would I?

76
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:55,040
Honestly.

77
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:58,460
But for such a rickety old doll,

78
00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:00,480
who'd pay 50,000 yen?
I can't understand that guy.

79
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:02,100
There really are, aren't there.

80
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:05,080
Those kinds of otaku, or rather maniacs,

81
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:07,020
or the Anything Appraisal Team types,

82
00:06:07,460 --> 00:06:10,840
treasure-hunting shows are all the rage these days,
after all.

83
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:13,460
Thanks for the meal.

84
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:16,420
Nakagawa, we're going on patrol.

85
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:19,580
What's gotten into you all of a sudden?

86
00:06:19,580 --> 00:06:21,600
Is it wrong for a police
officer to go on patrol?

87
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:24,060
No, no, it's not wrong, but...

88
00:06:24,660 --> 00:06:27,120
Then stop nitpicking and get the car ready.

89
00:06:27,700 --> 00:06:27,980
Yes.

90
00:06:30,380 --> 00:06:33,720
Well then, Officer Ryotsu,
we're off on patrol, sir!

91
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:35,860
O-okay.

92
00:06:38,340 --> 00:06:41,000
For Ryo-chan to go on
patrol of his own accord,

93
00:06:41,460 --> 00:06:43,200
it's like it's going to snow today,
isn't it?

94
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:49,940
Patrol, my foot. It's obviously a lie.

95
00:06:51,380 --> 00:06:55,120
To see the president of a toy company that specializes in dolls,
in Koiwa.

96
00:06:55,940 --> 00:06:58,900
So it's about making money after all?

97
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:02,080
Think about it. Dolls make money.

98
00:07:03,820 --> 00:07:05,300
It's awfully quiet, though.

99
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:09,900
Back in the day, you could hear
the machinery from a kilometer away.

100
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:17,560
Wait!

101
00:07:20,100 --> 00:07:22,160
We don't have a single
yen left in the house!

102
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:25,320
Even the machines here have all been seized.

103
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:27,360
What are you doing, Mr. President?

104
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:28,920
Ryo-san.

105
00:07:29,540 --> 00:07:35,440
The dolls we made for last Christmas, betting the company's fortune on them,
aren't selling at all.

106
00:07:36,380 --> 00:07:41,860
Debts keep piling up, we can't pay salaries, and the staff keep quitting.
We're on the verge of bankruptcy.

107
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:44,500
How many of the dolls we made are in stock?

108
00:07:44,820 --> 00:07:47,640
They've all been taken to pay off the debts.

109
00:07:48,080 --> 00:07:49,040
What a disaster.

110
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:52,640
What kind of doll was the
company's fortune riding on?

111
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:53,940
This one.

112
00:07:54,580 --> 00:07:56,260
What's this old lady doll?

113
00:07:56,660 --> 00:08:00,900
It's a Babafy doll,
made to cash in on the popular Puffy.

114
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:06,440
The real ones wiggle their hips
side to side like jellyfish,

115
00:08:06,440 --> 00:08:09,440
but this one's an old woman,
so her hips are bent over.

116
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:12,360
Who would buy such a worthless thing?

117
00:08:12,940 --> 00:08:15,760
No wonder the company's going
under if that's what you make.

118
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:19,360
I thought it would sell.

119
00:08:20,400 --> 00:08:23,700
If this goes on,
we'll lose the land and the building too,

120
00:08:23,700 --> 00:08:26,160
and my family will be
left out on the street.

121
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:29,500
Don't cry. Leave it to me to sort this out.

122
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:31,300
Please don't give me false comfort.

123
00:08:31,300 --> 00:08:33,380
The debt is fifty million yen, you know.

124
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:35,960
Ryo-san, you don't have that kind of money!

125
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:38,320
Who said anything about lending money?

126
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:41,840
I'll come up with a doll that sells.

127
00:08:42,420 --> 00:08:45,840
Even if you're my senior,
when it comes to dolls you're an amateur.

128
00:08:46,420 --> 00:08:48,440
You shouldn't make promises so lightly.

129
00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:49,840
Don't worry.

130
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:54,340
I may be an amateur with dolls,
but leave the money-making know-how to me.

131
00:08:55,060 --> 00:08:56,180
Really?

132
00:08:56,680 --> 00:08:59,600
First, the current
state of the doll industry

133
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:02,180
and research into what's selling well.

134
00:09:03,380 --> 00:09:04,480
Excuse me.

135
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:05,160
Yes?

136
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:08,580
Welcome!

137
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:11,020
I have something I'd
like to consult you about.

138
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:12,960
Well, come this way.

139
00:09:27,880 --> 00:09:29,840
Did you collect all of these yourself?

140
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:30,900
Of course.

141
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:34,220
Even the GI Jo and Combat Jo series,
this many too?

142
00:09:34,220 --> 00:09:35,600
Wow.

143
00:09:36,420 --> 00:09:37,600
This is GI Jo.

144
00:09:39,440 --> 00:09:42,960
Isn't that the Japanese Soldier,
the one said to be a rare, legendary piece?

145
00:09:43,400 --> 00:09:47,160
The Japanese Soldier was never sold in Japan,
you know.

146
00:09:47,160 --> 00:09:49,820
They even have GI Nurse?

147
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:53,160
These are all the kind that
would make collectors drool.

148
00:09:54,700 --> 00:09:57,860
You seem to have professional-level
knowledge when it comes to GI Jo.

149
00:09:58,540 --> 00:10:00,700
You've got quite a lot of the Birdy series too,
haven't you.

150
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:01,520
Yeah.

151
00:10:02,340 --> 00:10:04,520
Thanks to buying them
from Ryo-san last night,

152
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:06,740
I've now got the complete Birdy series.

153
00:10:06,740 --> 00:10:08,940
Which one is the doll I sold you?

154
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:10,080
This one.

155
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:12,680
It's practically brand new!

156
00:10:13,340 --> 00:10:15,520
I did proper maintenance on it, you know.

157
00:10:16,740 --> 00:10:19,560
Aren't these four figures all the same?

158
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:21,460
They look like it.

159
00:10:21,460 --> 00:10:24,240
I suppose an amateur
couldn't tell them apart.

160
00:10:31,800 --> 00:10:35,720
Well, if you look closely, the facial
expressions and finish are slightly different.

161
00:10:35,720 --> 00:10:37,660
I can't believe you can tell the difference.

162
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:43,180
You've got what it takes
to become a Birdy maniac.

163
00:10:43,620 --> 00:10:46,760
You change your personality sometimes,
don't you?

164
00:10:48,700 --> 00:10:51,040
So, what did you want to consult me about?

165
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:54,960
This gentleman here is the
president of Tateishi Toys.

166
00:10:55,960 --> 00:10:58,600
You're the company that released the
Babafy doll at the end of last year.

167
00:10:59,780 --> 00:11:00,980
You know about it?

168
00:11:00,980 --> 00:11:03,460
Of course, I bought one.

169
00:11:06,620 --> 00:11:08,180
Even as a collector,

170
00:11:08,500 --> 00:11:10,660
how could you buy such a worthless doll?

171
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:13,840
Well, I do collect oddball items too.

172
00:11:14,940 --> 00:11:17,760
But that kind of thing isn't
popular even among collectors, is it?

173
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:18,760
Just as I thought.

174
00:11:19,140 --> 00:11:22,720
Because we made that doll,
the company is about to go under.

175
00:11:23,500 --> 00:11:24,260
So, that's why -

176
00:11:24,260 --> 00:11:26,420
With Yano-kun's advice,

177
00:11:26,420 --> 00:11:28,880
we want to make dolls that sell.

178
00:11:30,540 --> 00:11:31,180
Understood.

179
00:11:32,760 --> 00:11:34,540
Please, let me help.

180
00:11:34,540 --> 00:11:35,200
Thank you.

181
00:11:36,860 --> 00:11:39,340
First, let's hear Ryo-san's thoughts.

182
00:11:40,080 --> 00:11:42,180
When it comes to
hit-selling dolls these days,

183
00:11:42,680 --> 00:11:45,240
I think it's got to be action figures.

184
00:11:45,240 --> 00:11:47,300
Action figures?

185
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:48,780
Action!

186
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:56,160
No!

187
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:59,020
It's not a figure skating figure.

188
00:11:59,480 --> 00:12:04,280
An action figure is a doll
whose body parts can be moved.

189
00:12:05,220 --> 00:12:06,880
Amateurs really are something.

190
00:12:07,660 --> 00:12:12,260
By the way,
GI Joe has 21 movable joints, right?

191
00:12:12,260 --> 00:12:12,740
Yeah.

192
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:17,120
With that one, you can't do the finishing
and painting as well as the Japanese ones.

193
00:12:17,540 --> 00:12:18,600
That's certainly true.

194
00:12:19,060 --> 00:12:21,720
That's the part that just isn't fun for me.

195
00:12:21,720 --> 00:12:22,280
I agree.

196
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:26,700
If they had more movable parts, you could do
interesting poses and it would be more fun, I think.

197
00:12:26,700 --> 00:12:27,380
Right, exactly.

198
00:12:29,020 --> 00:12:32,960
Right? Senpai, that's so true.

199
00:12:33,580 --> 00:12:39,600
Even Ryo-chan can't make a doll that becomes a trend overnight.
Who says it's impossible?

200
00:12:40,520 --> 00:12:49,140
Reiko, you're just talking big. Nothing is impossible for Ryotsu. So,
did you actually make it?

201
00:12:49,140 --> 00:12:55,200
Hear and be amazed, see and be astonished!
The ultimate figure I made is this!

202
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:00,200
W-what is this!

203
00:13:00,740 --> 00:13:02,220
It's wonderful!

204
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:06,420
Ryo-san has gotten his ticket to success.

205
00:13:19,760 --> 00:13:22,340
Y-you made this doll yourself?

206
00:13:22,520 --> 00:13:25,080
I call it Sergeant Ryo-san.

207
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:27,240
But isn't it cute?

208
00:13:29,020 --> 00:13:30,340
I wanted it to look just like me,

209
00:13:30,340 --> 00:13:32,720
but to make it a huge
hit like the Tamagotchi,

210
00:13:32,720 --> 00:13:35,380
it has to appeal to middle
and high school girls too.

211
00:13:35,380 --> 00:13:36,860
That's the right idea.

212
00:13:36,860 --> 00:13:38,440
For celebrities, hair is life.

213
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:40,800
They say a doll's face is its life,
after all.

214
00:13:41,520 --> 00:13:42,800
Don't be surprised just yet.

215
00:13:42,800 --> 00:13:46,240
This doll has another
superb feature built in.

216
00:13:46,820 --> 00:13:48,720
C-can it even form constellations?

217
00:13:48,720 --> 00:13:50,200
Constellations are just the start.

218
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:51,640
It can even sit cross-legged.

219
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:54,260
Like this.

220
00:13:54,260 --> 00:13:54,940
Amazing.

221
00:13:54,940 --> 00:13:58,080
It has remained the
king of the figure world.

222
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:00,840
Yet GI Joe can't do actions like this.

223
00:14:00,840 --> 00:14:01,780
Of course not.

224
00:14:02,480 --> 00:14:04,920
GI Joe only articulates at 21 points,

225
00:14:04,920 --> 00:14:09,100
but Sergeant Ryo-san can
articulate at a whopping 40 points!

226
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:10,340
40 points.

227
00:14:16,340 --> 00:14:20,580
I added joints to the knee hinges,
so it can bend this far.

228
00:14:20,580 --> 00:14:23,740
I also added three more movable parts,

229
00:14:23,740 --> 00:14:27,180
and made it movable in every direction,
so it can even sit cross-legged.

230
00:14:27,180 --> 00:14:28,460
Amazing!

231
00:14:29,020 --> 00:14:31,480
It can even do a 180-degree split.

232
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:33,740
This is revolutionary.

233
00:14:33,740 --> 00:14:37,000
But this will make the cost go up.

234
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:37,620
Idiot!

235
00:14:37,620 --> 00:14:39,400
No matter how much it costs,

236
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:43,500
a figure with 40 movable points, the
first in the world, will be a selling point.

237
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:45,080
Exactly.

238
00:14:45,080 --> 00:14:47,940
Collectors will definitely buy it,
even if it's a bit pricey.

239
00:14:47,940 --> 00:14:49,280
There's more!

240
00:14:49,280 --> 00:14:51,580
I used the same hinges in the hands,

241
00:14:52,160 --> 00:14:55,460
so it can even pinch the inner corner of the eye,
which was previously considered impossible,

242
00:14:55,460 --> 00:14:58,060
and I made the index
finger move independently.

243
00:14:59,020 --> 00:15:08,140
It can even hold things, and the
"dōmo dōmo" hand shape is recreated perfectly. This is incredible, it's guaranteed to sell!

244
00:15:08,820 --> 00:15:17,600
Let's spread the word to doll maniacs online right away. I'll handle it.
That's great! Alright, President, get this into production.

245
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:28,260
Wait, Ryo-san, I'd love to make it, but we don't have a single yen at home for upfront costs.
Don't worry. Are you fine with the president's family ending up on the street?

246
00:15:29,020 --> 00:15:30,760
Do you have no blood or tears in you?

247
00:15:31,320 --> 00:15:32,800
Fine, fine.

248
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:36,240
Let's have our company talk to the bank.

249
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:38,240
President, we've got the money!

250
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:40,580
All right,
then let's get started right away.

251
00:15:40,580 --> 00:15:42,000
Let's settle the pay.

252
00:15:42,920 --> 00:15:45,840
My cut is this much per unit. How's that?

253
00:15:46,420 --> 00:15:47,220
This much?

254
00:15:47,220 --> 00:15:50,660
If you don't like it, we can pretend
this whole conversation never happened.

255
00:15:51,080 --> 00:15:51,480
No way...

256
00:15:52,820 --> 00:15:55,980
Senpai gets really tough
when money's involved.

257
00:16:00,020 --> 00:16:03,020
Aaaaaah!

258
00:16:13,780 --> 00:16:17,860
Now, Ryo-san has chosen this lesson for us.

259
00:16:19,360 --> 00:16:23,400
Here you go, right this way.
Yes, thank you very much.

260
00:16:25,860 --> 00:16:28,400
Ryo-san's doll is a huge hit!

261
00:16:28,820 --> 00:16:31,660
The second and third
releases also sold like crazy.

262
00:16:39,240 --> 00:16:41,260
Today's "Visit the President's Home" segment

263
00:16:41,260 --> 00:16:43,020
is featuring the super-popular

264
00:16:43,020 --> 00:16:44,820
maker of Sergeant Ryo-san.

265
00:16:44,820 --> 00:16:47,220
Tateishi Toys' President Tateishi's

266
00:16:47,220 --> 00:16:48,880
We're broadcasting live from in
front of the company's own building.

267
00:16:49,740 --> 00:16:51,840
President, what a magnificent building!

268
00:16:54,400 --> 00:16:55,560
It's all thanks to you.

269
00:16:58,060 --> 00:16:58,700
That's amazing, isn't it?

270
00:16:59,260 --> 00:17:00,860
Not only did they pay off their debts,

271
00:17:00,860 --> 00:17:02,720
but they even built their own headquarters!

272
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:05,160
I never imagined it would be such a hit.

273
00:17:05,760 --> 00:17:06,840
Everyone,

274
00:17:06,840 --> 00:17:08,560
after all, has a Ryotsu doll.

275
00:17:08,560 --> 00:17:09,500
It's just too much.

276
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:10,820
Ryo-chan.

277
00:17:10,820 --> 00:17:12,820
I wonder how much money he made.

278
00:17:13,620 --> 00:17:15,800
He was demanding quite a fee, you know.

279
00:17:16,320 --> 00:17:16,960
100 million yen.

280
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:19,400
No, I'd bet it's closer to a billion yen.

281
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:34,480
You're the one who was hired when
your senior won the lottery, right?

282
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:36,700
I'm Sheep Sato.

283
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:39,720
I've been hired by the master once again.

284
00:17:40,660 --> 00:17:42,980
"Master"? You don't mean...

285
00:17:48,300 --> 00:17:51,480
Ryotsu! What's with that shabby outfit?

286
00:17:52,810 --> 00:17:56,160
I'd prefer you stop calling
me by my surname, Chief.

287
00:17:56,460 --> 00:17:56,820
What?

288
00:17:57,600 --> 00:18:01,160
I've decided to quit the
police force as of today.

289
00:18:01,460 --> 00:18:04,560
And from now on, yes, master.

290
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:06,080
Dinner is served.

291
00:18:07,260 --> 00:18:08,720
Vice President and…

292
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:09,780
in charge of planning.

293
00:18:09,920 --> 00:18:10,640
Executive?

294
00:18:11,100 --> 00:18:12,660
Well, that's how it is, so

295
00:18:12,660 --> 00:18:17,840
so you should all call me Vice President Ryotsu,
or Lord Ryotsu.

296
00:18:17,840 --> 00:18:19,480
You really are something!

297
00:18:20,460 --> 00:18:21,760
What is all this money!

298
00:18:21,840 --> 00:18:23,780
It's a thank-you for all your help.

299
00:18:24,720 --> 00:18:29,320
I'm planning to treat Reiko
and Nakagawa to an overseas trip.

300
00:18:29,320 --> 00:18:30,520
No thank you!

301
00:18:30,700 --> 00:18:35,380
If you have this much money, why don't you pay
back the debt you racked up from the lottery!

302
00:18:35,880 --> 00:18:37,980
Yeah, you've got a billion yen or so, right?

303
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:43,100
This is exactly why small-fry
common folk are such a pain.

304
00:18:43,100 --> 00:18:47,720
I'm not the kind of man who's satisfied
with a mere couple billion or so.

305
00:18:47,720 --> 00:18:50,400
I'll invest all the
profits into my next project,

306
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:54,940
and I plan to make ten times,
no, a hundred times that amount.

307
00:18:58,760 --> 00:18:59,560
What is this?

308
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:03,800
This is the next new project,
made with every last yen of our profits.

309
00:19:07,100 --> 00:19:09,900
It's the world's first
life-size action figure!

310
00:19:10,960 --> 00:19:13,280
It's impressive...
or rather, kind of creepy.

311
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:15,880
Does the expression change?

312
00:19:15,880 --> 00:19:18,300
It wasn't possible at 1/6 scale, but

313
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:20,640
at life-size, it became possible!

314
00:19:21,240 --> 00:19:23,180
But unlike the 1/6 scale figures,

315
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:24,920
it's just too creepy.

316
00:19:25,340 --> 00:19:26,420
That's not true at all.

317
00:19:26,840 --> 00:19:29,580
Since it's life-size,
it can even wear real clothes.

318
00:19:30,280 --> 00:19:31,640
That's true, but

319
00:19:32,220 --> 00:19:34,320
if you don't sell this
at a pretty high price,

320
00:19:34,320 --> 00:19:35,840
won't you fail to break even?

321
00:19:35,840 --> 00:19:36,820
Exactly.

322
00:19:36,820 --> 00:19:38,860
I've set the list price at 300,000 yen.

323
00:19:39,340 --> 00:19:40,280
300,000 yen?

324
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:41,840
That's way too expensive.

325
00:19:41,840 --> 00:19:44,240
At that price, nobody's going to buy it.

326
00:19:44,740 --> 00:19:45,800
I'm telling you this for your own good.

327
00:19:45,800 --> 00:19:47,020
Just don't do that.

328
00:19:47,020 --> 00:19:49,280
I'll talk to the police somehow

329
00:19:49,280 --> 00:19:51,620
and make sure you can keep
working just as before.

330
00:19:51,620 --> 00:19:53,380
Stop!

331
00:19:53,380 --> 00:19:56,400
Amateurs are always like this

332
00:19:56,800 --> 00:19:58,560
Figures are eternal and indestructible.

333
00:19:59,140 --> 00:20:02,920
With this, I'll become the
Bill Gates of the doll world.

334
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:04,740
Hahahaha!

335
00:20:13,720 --> 00:20:18,000
World's first full-scale action figure,
Sergeant Ryo-san

336
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:20,960
Now released worldwide simultaneously.

337
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:23,720
The full-scale figure has been released.

338
00:20:37,320 --> 00:20:38,480
It didn't sell at all.

339
00:20:44,580 --> 00:20:47,740
At this rate,
we'll go bust with a mountain of stock.

340
00:20:47,740 --> 00:20:50,160
Ryo-san, do something!

341
00:20:51,900 --> 00:20:53,160
Leave it to me.

342
00:21:02,520 --> 00:21:03,740
What is this?

343
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:06,340
With this, it's bound to sell.

344
00:21:17,640 --> 00:21:20,580
Bundling it with Ryo-chan
is a bit insulting.

345
00:21:20,580 --> 00:21:22,960
In business, as long as it sells,
anything goes.

346
00:21:25,020 --> 00:21:27,720
There's a line at the
shoe store over there too.

347
00:21:27,720 --> 00:21:31,480
That? That's my Shibuya-style version.

348
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:33,720
Shibuya-style version?

349
00:21:34,780 --> 00:21:37,800
Bundling it with the hugely
popular premium sneakers

350
00:21:38,820 --> 00:21:42,580
It's like those hero-themed snacks with a
toy inside that were popular back in the day.

351
00:21:44,360 --> 00:21:46,040
This will clear out all the stock.

352
00:21:46,040 --> 00:21:48,580
Let's go all out and hit the Ginza,
Mr. President!

353
00:21:48,580 --> 00:21:51,180
If we're going to party,
let's drink it up in Akasaka, Ginza-style.

354
00:21:57,380 --> 00:21:58,680
Can't go, can't go!

355
00:21:58,680 --> 00:22:00,780
Come on, Reiko, you too, get inside!

356
00:22:00,780 --> 00:22:03,740
Is it really okay to keep going like this?

357
00:22:04,760 --> 00:22:09,060
Nothing the senior officer does has ever gone smoothly to the end,
you know.

358
00:22:11,440 --> 00:22:12,820
Yes, this is Nakagawa speaking.

359
00:22:13,880 --> 00:22:14,980
Unnatural death body!

360
00:22:15,800 --> 00:22:16,240
What?

361
00:22:16,240 --> 00:22:21,300
Chief, the suspicious body is...

362
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:23,280
It's that, that thing.

363
00:22:26,780 --> 00:22:31,160
Isn't that my figure?

364
00:22:31,160 --> 00:22:32,880
What do you mean?

365
00:22:34,040 --> 00:22:36,100
Yes, we got testimony from an eyewitness.

366
00:22:36,660 --> 00:22:40,020
The customers who bought the
bundled doll with the sneakers,

367
00:22:40,380 --> 00:22:42,580
after taking only the
female doll and the sneakers,

368
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:44,780
reportedly threw away the male doll.

369
00:22:45,460 --> 00:22:46,020
What?!

370
00:22:46,680 --> 00:22:48,340
Everyone's after the bundled ones,

371
00:22:48,340 --> 00:22:50,920
so it's the bundle dolls
and sneakers they want

372
00:22:50,920 --> 00:22:51,600
Hey, look!

373
00:22:52,380 --> 00:22:53,960
The dolls keep coming down the line!

374
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:08,020
They stopped selling.

375
00:23:13,140 --> 00:23:16,380
If we'd only made the
1/6 scale figures alone,

376
00:23:21,560 --> 00:23:23,360
N-no way.

377
00:23:23,360 --> 00:23:25,460
I never expected it to come to this much.

378
00:23:25,460 --> 00:23:27,780
The cost of hauling away these dolls

379
00:23:27,780 --> 00:23:29,480
you're going to pay for, you hear me?

380
00:23:29,480 --> 00:23:29,940
No way...

381
00:23:30,440 --> 00:23:32,300
The company has gone bankrupt,

382
00:23:32,300 --> 00:23:35,580
and I'm not getting a single yen from it!

383
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:40,820
It's no use tagging along. You're not a police officer anymore,
you know.

384
00:23:40,820 --> 00:23:43,300
No, that was just a joke!

385
00:23:43,300 --> 00:23:50,180
I don't know anything about it. Those dolls have to be cleared out today or they'll charge us,
so make sure you dispose of them properly, got it?

386
00:23:51,580 --> 00:23:52,800
That's unreasonable!

387
00:23:54,380 --> 00:23:56,360
The dolls came crashing down on me!

388
00:23:57,180 --> 00:23:57,980
Chief

389
00:24:03,460 --> 00:24:04,260
Chief

390
00:24:04,260 --> 00:24:08,100
I'll be the organizer for the Katsushika
station's company trip this time.

391
00:24:08,100 --> 00:24:10,060
Hey, what's with that suspicious look?

392
00:24:10,400 --> 00:24:12,800
I'll charter a super luxurious cruiser,

393
00:24:12,800 --> 00:24:17,620
and let everyone enjoy fishing and a fancy
meal with a live band to their heart's content.

394
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:21,520
Next time:
"Torrent Hall Ship Panic," see you then.

395
00:24:30,620 --> 00:24:37,320
Though rumors say I'm a
woman who can't fall in love,

396
00:24:37,320 --> 00:24:41,940
there are mountains of things I want to do.

397
00:24:41,940 --> 00:24:52,020
I want to ride a motorbike
across the vast desert.

398
00:24:52,020 --> 00:24:59,260
I want to be freer than a bird.

399
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:07,120
A lady's dreams change
as fast as a kaleidoscope.

400
00:25:07,120 --> 00:25:07,560
me

401
00:25:09,500 --> 00:25:10,200
me

402
